AA financial commercial-paper curve x NASDAQ, 1998-01-05 .. 2026-07-02, n = 4396
   days with dX_t = 0 exactly (curve unchanged): 15 (0.3%) -- these carry no direction, and the
   zero-norm convention t_theta(0) := 0 drops them from the score.

1. TAIL INDEX OF ||dX_t||, and is it one episode?
   full sample                        n= 4396  point=1.597  95% [1.336, 2.171]   straddles 2
   excluding 2007-2009                n= 3701  point=1.830  95% [1.442, 2.372]   straddles 2
   excluding 2008 alone               n= 4180  point=1.879  95% [1.537, 2.400]   straddles 2
   2010 onward only                   n= 1456  point=1.694  95% [1.186, 2.818]   straddles 2
   pre-2007 only                      n= 2245  point=1.880  95% [1.522, 2.503]   straddles 2
   responses, for reference -- these must stay ABOVE 2 for theta=1 to help,
   since tr V_1 = E eps^2 is the one moment the theorem does need:
   |Y_t| NASDAQ return                n= 4396  point=2.573  95% [2.259, 3.216]
   |Y_t| VIX log change               n= 4396  point=2.553  95% [2.206, 2.992]

2. DOES tr Vhat SETTLE?  Theorem 6' says tr V_0 = E[eps^2 ||X||^2] has
   nothing to converge to when the index is below 2, while tr V_1 = E eps^2
   does.  Expanding subsamples, H0: beta = 0, Panel A.
         n      tr V(th=0.0)     tr V(th=0.5)     tr V(th=1.0)
       879              1917             74.8            5.802
      1758              1676            53.15            4.466
      2637              1265            40.75            3.344
      3516              4984            70.23            3.387
      4396         5.559e+04            213.5            3.962
   -> a column that keeps climbing has no population limit; one that
      settles does.  This is the diagnostic, on real data.

